  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I could not run `vite build` or open the page in a browser, so the render is untested.\n\n- **Placement:** 8,000 trees and 2,000 rocks are scattered over a 60 m radius disc, using a mulberry32 generator with a fixed seed, so the forest is the same on every load.\n- **Instancing:** the scene draws through four instanced nodes plus the ground plane. Trunks are cylinders, canopies are cones, and rocks are low-poly icosahedrons.\n- **Colour:** each instance has its own colour. Canopies vary from yellow-green to blue-green, trunks vary in brown, and rocks vary in grey. The materials are white so the instance colours show through.\n- **Light and fog:** there is one shadow-casting directional light, with a 4096 map and 3 cascades reaching 220 m. A hemisphere light adds fill. `effects.fog` gives exponential-squared fog (density 0.005), and the background uses the fog colour.\n- **Camera:** it circles the forest once every 90 seconds at radius 105 m and height 62 m. A 45° field of view should keep the whole disc in frame at every angle. The orbit works by changing the camera's position every frame. The engine's camera controller is a stub with default settings, so `setPose` would do nothing.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` resolves and three animation frames have passed.\n- **Shadow bias:** I picked the values by estimate (`bias` 0.0005, `normalBias` 0.05). If the shadows show acne or detach from the trees, these are the first values to adjust.\n\n",
  "finalTypecheckPass": true,
